This program first asks the user to type in some text, and then outputs the grade level for the text, according to the Coleman-Liau formula.
Main Function: The main function prompts the user for a text input, calculates the reading level using the calculate_reading_level function, and then prints the reading level using the print_reading_level function.
Letter, Word, and Sentence Count Functions: These functions count the number of letters, words, and sentences in the text, respectively. They loop through each character in the text and use conditions to update the counters.
Calculate Reading Level Function: This function calculates the reading level index using the counts from the previous functions. It uses the Coleman-Liau index formula, which involves the average number of letters and 
  sentences per 100 words.
Print Reading Level Function: This function prints the reading level based on the index. It handles special cases for very low or high reading levels.
